(Customer Self-Service Portal - Requirements Overview) Tj
T*
T*
(OVERVIEW) Tj
T*
(This document captures the requirements for a new customer self-service portal for a) Tj
T*
(regional insurer client of BISTEC Global. Policyholders will use the portal to view policy) Tj
T*
(documents, file and track claims, and update contact and billing details without calling) Tj
T*
(the contact centre.) Tj
T*
T*
(SCOPE AND USERS) Tj
T*
(The portal must support approximately 20,000 registered policyholders at launch, with) Tj
T*
(headroom for growth as the insurer migrates further policy lines onto the platform. Peak) Tj
T*
(concurrent usage is expected around monthly billing cycles and renewal periods, so the) Tj
T*
(system should handle bursty traffic without manual intervention.) Tj
T*
T*
(AUTHENTICATION) Tj
T*
(Corporate staff and agents will sign in with the insurer's existing Microsoft 365 tenant) Tj
T*
(via single sign-on \(SSO\); policyholders will use a separate, portal-specific login. The) Tj
T*
(authentication design should reuse BISTEC's default Microsoft identity platform) Tj
T*
(integration rather than a bespoke identity provider.) Tj
T*
T*
(BUDGET AND TIMELINE) Tj
T*
(The client has stated a tight budget for this engagement and prefers to reuse managed) Tj
T*
(cloud services over self-hosted infrastructure wherever the cost difference is) Tj
T*
(significant. A first release is targeted within one quarter, covering policy viewing and) Tj
T*
(claims status only; billing updates and document uploads can follow in a later phase.) Tj
T*
T*
(TEAM AND DELIVERY) Tj
T*
(The insurer's in-house engineering team is a .NET team with several years of experience) Tj
T*
(running ASP.NET Core services in Azure, and would maintain the solution after handover.) Tj
T*
(BISTEC will pair with the client team during delivery so that ownership can transfer) Tj
T*
(smoothly at the end of the engagement.) Tj
T*
T*
(COMPLIANCE) Tj
T*
(The portal processes personal and policy data for EU-resident customers, so the solution) Tj
T*
(must meet GDPR requirements for data minimisation, consent, and the right to erasure.) Tj
T*
(Audit logging of access to policy and claims records is required for the insurer's) Tj
T*
(compliance reporting.) Tj
T*
T*
(NON-FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS) Tj
T*
(The portal should remain available during the insurer's business hours with no planned) Tj
T*
(downtime for routine deployments. Response times for common actions such as viewing a) Tj
T*
(policy or checking claim status should stay under two seconds under normal load.) Tj
T*
